Hypervisor: make the default of spec.highAvailability configurable

HypervisorController.Reconcile in internal/controller/
hypervisor_controller.go builds every Hypervisor it creates from a
literal with HighAvailability: true. In the Handover phase,
OnboardingController.completeOnboarding returns without a requeue while
spec.highAvailability is true and the HaEnabled condition is not, and
only an HA service (SAP's kvm-ha-service) sets that condition. Where no
such service runs, onboarding never finishes until someone patches the
field to false on every Hypervisor, again for each node that joins
later and for each Hypervisor that is recreated.

The --default-high-availability flag (default true, the behaviour
without the flag) sets the value the controller writes on create. The
flag is read on create only, so an existing Hypervisor keeps its value.
The literal in hypervisor_taint_controller.go stays: that controller
only reads into it.

No upstream test pins the created spec. The patch adds
TestHypervisorCreatedWithDefaultHighAvailability, a plain Go test
outside the Ginkgo suite with controller-runtime's fake client, so it
runs without envtest; the CobaltCore image build runs it and fails
when it does not pass.

Applies-to: cobaltcore-dev/openstack-hypervisor-operator main @ a2baf3f4002e39ff93f105fae9594b357ba55b21

Upstream status: not submitted

